---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`The twelve-week teaching schedule: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Each week below pairs a lecture with a session. The lecture argues for a
    preparation decision; the session is where it is exercised, not restated.
    Seven sessions — weeks 2, 3, 4, 5, 8, 9 and 10 — run a calculator against
    figures for an ingredient the student chooses: a macronutrient split in
    weeks 2, 3, 4 and 9, a safe-until time in weeks 5, 8 and 10. Three of the
    remaining five sit at the bench instead of on screen. Week 7 checks a
    knife's grip and edge against reference figures for hardness and angle.
    Week 11
    applies heat for the first time, to test whether preparation rather than
    technique decides the result. Week 12 rehearses that same test under the
    conditions of the graded practical that follows it. Weeks 1 and 6 carry
    no exercise at all, and each says why. A session with nothing yet to
    exercise runs no calculator; a lecture with no session behind it would go
    untested.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
